---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// The root of `new.southvillerunningclub.co.uk` — the front door the club website will
// eventually be, and for now a holding page that says so.
//
// It states no date. When the new site replaces the old one is a committee decision and
// [a factual claim not to be invented](../../../../docs/architecture/principles.md#stop-and-ask).
---

<Base
  title="Southville Running Club — a new website is on the way"
  description="The club's new website, being built around race sign-ups and race timing."
>
  {
    /* Just the club's name. The banner directly above already welcomes the visitor to the
      new website, and a heading one line below saying the same thing again reads as a
      site that is nervous. The page still needs an h1 — dropping it outright is an
      accessibility failure, not a tidy-up. */
  }
  <h1>Southville Running Club</h1>

  <p class="lede">The club's new website is being built here, a piece at a time.</p>

  <p>Two parts of it are already here:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/nn/"><strong>Nightingale Nightmare</strong></a> — the race, and its sign-up
    </li>
    {
      /* **No link to `/timing`**, since 11 September 2026. It is staff-only now and
      answers 404 to everybody else, so linking it from the club's front page would send
      a runner to a page that says there is nothing there. Race results, when there are
      some to show, belong on the race's own year page. */
    }
  </ul>

  {
    /* What was here before — "nothing that is already working will move" — was true of
      the paths and false of the address, which is the only part a member sees. The whole
      site moves to southvillerunningclub.co.uk at the cutover. Saying otherwise is a
      promise the club would have to break. */
  }
  <p>
    The rest of the club's website will be added here as it is built. When it is all here,
    this becomes the club's main website.
  </p>

  <footer>
    <p>Southville Running Club.</p>
  </footer>
</Base>
